// label.rule -- SYNTHETIC (NO vendor data). Exercises text/label handling
// (fork feature #24): TEXT/LABEL/ATTACH/PORT layers wired to NET NAMES, plus the
// label-short electrical check built on top of them.
//
// Layer numbers are synthetic placeholders:
//   poly 2/0  cont 3/0  met1 4/0   |   netname 40/0 (TEXT shapes)
//
//   LABEL <text-layer> <conductor-layer>
//       attaches the text shapes on <text-layer> to <conductor-layer>'s nets as
//       NET NAMES (db::LayoutToNetlist::connect(Region, Texts)), so an extracted
//       net carries the designer's name instead of $1/$2. ATTACH and PORT are
//       accepted as synonyms.
//
//   ERC SHORT <text-layer>
//       ONE extracted net carrying TWO DIFFERENT names is a label short / net
//       name clash -- the two nets the designer named separately are physically
//       one. Count = the number of such nets; the marker is the whole shorted
//       net, so the debug geometry is the conductor to cut.
//       Two labels bearing the SAME string on one net are NOT a clash.

LAYER poly    2 0
LAYER cont    3 0
LAYER met1    4 0
LAYER netname 40 0

CONNECT poly met1 BY cont

LABEL netname met1

ERC.NAMESHORT {
  ERC SHORT netname
}
